Grain — Licensing

Copyright (c) 2026 Keaton Dunsford and contributors.

Grain carries two kinds of work under one roof, and each is offered under the
license that fits it. This file is the index; the full texts live beside it.

Code — Apache-2.0 OR MIT (your choice)

  Every source file, script, and build tool in this repository is offered
  under the Apache License 2.0 or the MIT License, at your option — the
  permissive dual-license convention the wider ecosystem already reads. Take
  whichever suits your use; you need satisfy only one.

    - Apache-2.0 — see LICENSE-APACHE
    - MIT        — see LICENSE-MIT

Documentation and prose — CC-BY-4.0

  The writings — research, design briefs, specifications, session logs, and
  the prose throughout active-designing/, external-research/, context/,
  work-in-progress/, expanding-prompts/, session-logs/, and SOURCE.md — are
  offered under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International license.
  Share and adapt them freely, for any purpose, with attribution.

    - CC-BY-4.0 — see LICENSE-CC-BY

Contributions

  Unless you state otherwise, work you contribute is offered under these same
  terms — code under Apache-2.0 OR MIT, prose under CC-BY-4.0 — so the tree
  stays licensed as a whole. Every commit is GPG-signed; the history proves who
  wrote it. See CONTRIBUTING.md for the shape a contribution takes.
